description: "Where Lightening Lives has run population and newborn screening for sickle cell anaemia and thalassaemia: 15 sites in nine states and Delhi. Photographs from the field and the laboratory."
label: Our work
h1: Where we have worked
lead: "Population and newborn screening at 15 sites in nine states and Delhi, with government programmes, hospitals and NGOs. We add to this page as the work goes on."
closing:
  h2: Planning work like this?
  body: Tell us the community, the condition and who you are working with.
  solid: { text: Partner with us, href: /partners/ }
  line: { text: For programmes, href: /partners/#programmes }
---
{#- Our work (content file 5.11), the company's field record. The layout opens the page (label, h1,
    lead) and closes it with the band whose words are above; 5.11 has no notice. The sites are 6.1's
    fifteen (src/site/_data/sites.json), grouped by state in 6.2's order (work.states): the state
    names the group and its towns follow as detail (R2). 6.2's line for each state stays on the map:
    six states share one, which the table would repeat (R1), and the marks say what was screened. A
    screening done is marked with the proof tag; one not done has nothing; no numbers of people. The [PLACEHOLDER] under the table is left out. The map is
    the home page's, opened on "Our work". Recent work has its heading, the kinds of entry and one
    line until the company sends photographs (Phase 7); "The photographs" is guidance for the company
    and is not rendered. The bands alternate back from the closing band's paper, so the first section
    stays on the opening's mist and continues its sheet. -#}
{%- from "map.njk" import mapSection with context %}
{#- The poster's five columns: the key in sites.json, and the name a mark carries. -#}
{%- set columns = [
  { key: "sca_pop", name: "Sickle cell anaemia, population" },
  { key: "sca_nb", name: "Sickle cell anaemia, newborn" },
  { key: "sbt_pop", name: "Sickle-beta thalassaemia, population" },
  { key: "sbt_nb", name: "Sickle-beta thalassaemia, newborn" },
  { key: "bt_pop", name: "Beta thalassaemia, population" }
] %}

  <!-- The sites: 6.1 grouped by state (R2). A table on a wide screen; on a phone, one entry per state -->
  <section id="sites" class="section" aria-labelledby="sites-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="sites-h" class="h2 max-w-[44rem]">Population and newborn screening, by state</h2>
      <table class="sites sites-states mt-12" aria-labelledby="sites-h">
        <colgroup><col class="sites-col-site"></colgroup>
        <colgroup span="2"></colgroup>
        <colgroup span="2"></colgroup>
        <colgroup span="1"></colgroup>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col" rowspan="2" class="sites-site-h">State</th>
            <th scope="colgroup" colspan="2">Sickle cell anaemia</th>
            <th scope="colgroup" colspan="2">Sickle-beta thalassaemia</th>
            <th scope="colgroup">Beta thalassaemia</th>
          </tr>
          <tr class="sites-kinds">
            <th scope="col">Population</th>
            <th scope="col">Newborn</th>
            <th scope="col">Population</th>
            <th scope="col">Newborn</th>
            <th scope="col">Population</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        {%- for state in work.states %}
        <tbody>
          {%- set here = sites | where("state", state.name) %}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{{ state.name }} <span class="sites-count">{{ here | length }} {{ "site" if (here | length) == 1 else "sites" }}</span></th>
            {%- for column in columns %}
            <td>{% if here | selectattr(column.key) | length %}<span class="tag tag-proof"><span class="mark-name">{{ column.name }}</span></span>{% endif %}</td>
            {%- endfor %}
          </tr>
        </tbody>
        {%- endfor %}
      </table>
      <p class="sites-thanks">We thank the participating individuals, clinicians and frontline health workers at every site.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The map, opened on "Our work": the nine states and Delhi (R2) -->
  {{ mapSection({ layer: "work", h2: "On the map", body: "Fifteen sites in nine states and Delhi, from Delhi in the north to Tamil Nadu in the south, and from Gujarat in the west to Jharkhand in the east. Most lie in the sickle cell belt across central India, where the need is greatest." }) }}

  <!-- Recent work: the kinds of entry, and none yet (the photographs wait for the company; Phase 7) -->
  <section id="recent" class="section" aria-labelledby="recent-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="recent-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Recent work</h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Photographs from our work are on their way.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="entries mt-10">
        <ul class="entries-kinds">
          <li class="label">In the field</li>
          <li class="label">In the laboratory</li>
          <li class="label">Training</li>
          <li class="label">With our partners</li>
          <li class="label">At a conference</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
